{"name":"Ghoul","hex":"#667744","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghoul","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A demon said to feed on corpses.","A graverobber. (Can we verify this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghoul"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghoul","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a ghoul is a demon-like being or monstrous humanoid, often associated with graveyards and the consumption of human flesh. The concept of the ghoul originated in pre-Islamic Arabian religion. Modern fiction often uses the term to label a specific kind of monster."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Amine_Discovered_with_the_Goule.jpg/330px-Amine_Discovered_with_the_Goule.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul","wikidata":"Q208446"},{"title":"Ghoul (miniseries)","blocks":[{"text":"Ghoul is an Indian horror television miniseries based on the Arab folklore monster ghoul, and the second Netflix original from India, after Sacred Games. The series is written and directed by Patrick Graham and jointly produced by Jason Blum, Anurag Kashyap, Ryan Turek, Vikramaditya Motwane, Michael Hogan, Kilian Kerwin, John Penotti and Suraj Gohill under their respective banners Blumhouse Productions, Phantom Films and Ivanhoe Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/Ghoul_-_2018_Poster.jpg/330px-Ghoul_-_2018_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul_(miniseries)","wikidata":"Q48673879"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Weird_Tales_v10n04_-_Pickman%27s_Model.png/500px-Weird_Tales_v10n04_-_Pickman%27s_Model.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Weird_Tales_v10n04_-_Pickman%27s_Model.png/1280px-Weir